# Hillman Minx four-door saloon, 1931-1935.
#
# The pre-war Minx: the 1,185 cc side-valve four in the six-light saloon
# body, with the upright grille and separate wings. The pack photographs a
# December 1932 car, registration JJ 1813.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillman_Minx
#
# Dimensions 3.404 x 1.473 x 1.753 m, wheelbase 2.337 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is about 20 degrees off side, not a true level
# profile; the flank is estimated from it and the other views. The
# limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, green, blue and
# maroon are plain names. Weights 8, 7, 5, 5, total 25, provisional.
#
# Speed 105 km/h. Comfort 45/398, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 45: a tall,
# upright 1930s saloon. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1931 intro, retires staggered 1953-1956.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/hillman-minx-pre-war.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/hillman-minx-pre-war.dae. References:
# citycars/references/hillman-minx-pre-war/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: image 1 is a shallow front angle, not a true side, and
# the rear is inferred. The running-board transitions and rear spare mounting are
# simplified; the 1934 car's later trim was not copied. At 128 px the six-light
# cabin, upright grille and separate wings read as a pre-war Minx.


obj=citycar
name=HillmanMinxPreWar(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=8
intro_year=1931
